θα(t) =α ∗ θ(t) + (1− α) ∗ θα(t − 1)
). The method introduces a novel teacher-dependent weighting scheme (λα) and incorporates multiview distillation using data augmentation. The overall loss combines Cross-Entropy with a Kullback-Leibler divergence term between the student and evolving teacher logits. The parameter α provides precise control over the plasticity-stability trade-off, and λα is empirically related to α by a linear logarithmic function (
λα = a∗log10(α)+b
). For inference, the final model parameters are derived by averaging the student and teacher weights (
θ⋆ = θS+θT 2
). The strategy is designed for seamless integration into existing OCL baselines.
